// ── TRACK 2 · LAYER 2 · MOTION ────────────────────────────────────────────
// The hook. One rigid 4-note cell — root, 5th, 3rd, 5th — hammered as 16ths
// and simply TRANSPOSED onto each chord. Keeping the shape identical is the
// whole point: when Dm slides to Eb in bar 2, every single note of the cell
// moves up a half or whole step at once. That parallel slide is the darksynth
// signature, and an ostinato that never varies its contour reads as machinery
// closing in rather than as a melody.
//
// The cell is inverted (5th-root-3rd-root, or 3rd-root-5th-root) in bars 5-7
// so the B section stays inside one octave instead of climbing off the top.
// Written as <[cell*4] ...> so each cycle gets exactly one chord's cell four
// times — the arp stays locked to the bass, one chord per cycle.
setcps(0.5)
stack(
  note(`<[[d5 a5 f5 a5]*4] [[eb5 bb5 g5 bb5]*4]
         [[d5 a5 f5 a5]*4] [[c5 g5 eb5 g5]*4]
         [[d5 g5 bb5 g5]*4] [[d5 bb5 f5 bb5]*4]
         [[eb5 bb5 g5 bb5]*4] [[d5 a5 f5 a5]*4]>`)
    .s("square")
    // Resonant sweep completing once per loop: the player learns the shape of
    // the 16 seconds without ever noticing they are being told where they are.
    // lpq 12 is high enough that the sweep screams at the corner — that whistle
    // is the aggression, and it costs nothing in headroom.
    .lpf(sine.range(650, 3100).slow(8)).lpq(12)
    .gain(0.115).release(0.04).attack(0.001)
    .delay(0.3).delaytime(0.1875).delayfeedback(0.34)   // dotted-16th smear
    .pan(0.57)
)
